course: dictionary
lesson: 9179
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the other words in the sentence tell you which one is meant. «Add soap and the grease slides away.» Grease slides away when you wash it, so soap here means the stuff you use with water to clean.
explain: Soap is a noun, a bar or a liquid you wash with. It is also a verb: to soap something is to rub soap on it. Check the sentence to see which one is meant. If the word is about washing or rubbing, it is the thing or the action.
explain: Soap has a third meaning. A soap, or soap opera, is a TV or radio story about the same people that goes on for years. The clue is the story: a soap is not something you wash with, but something you watch or listen to.
fact: Soap is a noun for the thing you wash with, such as a bar of soap or liquid soap.
fact: To soap something means to rub soap on it. The forms are soaps, soaped and soaping.
fact: «Washing hands with soap for about 20 seconds removes most germs.» Use soap and water for about 20 seconds before you eat and after the toilet.
fact: Soap breaks up grease and helps wash germs away.
fact: A soap opera is a TV or radio story about the same people that goes on for years.
exercise: «Add soap and the grease slides away.» What is soap in this sentence? | A kind of green plant | A bubble | *Something you use with water to wash | A TV story that goes on for years
exercise: Mia reads «Tonight's soap is about the same families as last year.» What is a soap here? | *A TV or radio story that goes on for years | A bar you wash with | A bubble in the sink | A tin of grease
exercise: Sam says, «I soaped the window.» What does soaped mean? | Made it wet with rain | Painted it | *Rubbed soap on it | Broke it into pieces
test: «Washing hands with soap for about 20 seconds removes most germs.» What does this tell you soap helps to do? | Make hands sticky | Keep hands cold | *Remove germs | Make a story on TV
test: Grandma says, «I'm going to soap the car.» What is she going to do? | Watch a soap opera | Write a story about cars | Drive the car to the shop | *Rub soap on the car
exam: Which sentence uses soap as a noun, meaning the thing itself? | «She soaped her hair in the bath.» | «Soap the bowl quickly.» | *«Please buy a new bar of soap.» | «Please soap the windows.»
